@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@
+# Household BR-02 and final App Shell — Dev-2 handoff
+
+2026-11-08. PO remains the only main merge coordinator.
+
+## Branches and ownership
+
+Initial fetched main: `43f3897aa2fca6828c4d0fe65531f3c71152b903`.
+Updated fetched main: `743b21f59937b3ca8dd066c1bfd5d966d241862b`.
+
+* BR-02 worktree `.worktrees/household-br02`, branch `integration/household-br02-local`.
+  Composite dependency base `5d20bd93dd36b46dd35fe26291c221781fdc8f5b`; own BR-02 commit
+  `e2edd3eedc650e49ae648358afe526cdea0edae9` (source + tests, no dependency source copied).
+* Full integration worktree `.worktrees/final-shell`, branch `integration/final-shell-local`.
+  Includes approved main UI/search/completion/hotfix and frozen #25, plus local dependency merges.
+  Latest dependency revision base: `e0f81e0f6a4215cbb7b1b2380be219be9dafc8f4`.
+* Clean review branch `feature/final-app-shell-integration` starts from main `743b21f...` in
+  `.worktrees/final-shell-review`. It contains only production composition/home copy and test changes;
+  BR-02 production UI and unmerged #25 source are excluded. Its regression is recorded separately.
+  Published as PR #27: https://github.com/ngocdg103/it3180-SE02/pull/27, verified source commit
+  `6ec8ee1013eefe3d79d426fa657770367273ea79` (694 normal / 695 smoke / 821 full MySQL, all PASS).
+
+All old worktrees and #20/#22/#23 local branches were preserved. No reset/clean/discard/force push.
+
+| Dependency | Frozen source | Contained in fetched main |
+|---|---|---|
+| #18 Billing UI | `9ab70d110a8c28158c40466533af5eb1bf9b137d` | yes |
+| #19 Notice | `070ca49cb281bc350829b4e3c270f4c6fd4648fc` | yes |
+| #21 Payment | `fb80bee6f85d01b12724b399c9f0ccdb318d670e` | yes |
+| #24 Debt | `399ad6b11312fc55d88c2ece5b9643ddf4df050c` | yes |
+| #25 BR-02 Billing history | `6339cf2e10a9090a39bab3461aa2d85f9d240a94` | **no — local integration only** |
+| Fee Rate hotfix | `8a5b1072646775e8cff6154adb14abc91ea65a77` | yes |
+
+Git ancestry verified the merged source commits; GitHub API still reported #18/#19 open at inspection despite
+their source commits being ancestors of main. Do not confuse API status with absence of the actual code.
+
+## BR-02 implementation (local until #25 is merged)
+
+Production HouseholdServiceImpl now receives `new BillingDAO(connections)` instead of ApartmentChargeLookup.NONE.
+The production BillingServiceImpl is supplied to HouseholdNavigator alongside ResidentService and ResidentSearchService.
+Search and Resident UI remain wired. Neither production BillingDAO/BillingService nor owner module code was edited.
+
+Household Detail includes a read-only invoice-history table: period, invoice ID, total VND, due date and area/people
+at billing time. It calls getApartmentHistory on a background Task, preserves newest-first results and never
+recalculates snapshots. With Payment already in main and the revised #25 handoff confirming the committed source,
+paid/owing/status columns now display daThanhToan/conThieu/trangThai directly from stored invoice headers. The UI
+only translates the provided enum label; it never derives a status from an absent payment integration or recomputes balances.
+The #25 revision changed no production Billing history contract; its new test proves committed partial/full Payment
+is reflected while billing input snapshots remain unchanged. Original frozen #25 was `6dbd784...`; revision is `6339cf2...`.
+
+DEBT_REPORT_VIEW is checked before loading and before applying a completed result. ADMIN/ACCOUNTANT can view;
+RESIDENT is denied both by Dashboard navigation and service authorization. Empty/error/retry are explicit and errors
+are sanitized. History busy state is ORed with Household and Resident activity. Dispose cancels the history Task,
+clears data and removes the busy listener; late callbacks cannot repopulate a detached panel.
+
+The existing area-change Alert now holds the module busy while confirmation is pending. Save/cancel are guarded,
+the exact submitted payload is reused only after OK, and Cancel makes no confirmed update. Shell navigation/logout
+therefore remain locked during both the write and confirmation. No Scene/Stage or AuthenticationNavigator changes.
+
+## Final module composition
+
+* FeeRateModule.registration — FEE_RATE_VIEW (real owner hotfix, no fabricated busy property).
+* BillingModule.registration and NoticeModule.registration — DEBT_REPORT_VIEW.
+* ReceiptModule.open — PAYMENT_HISTORY_VIEW_ALL, per its handoff. PAYMENT_RECORD remains ACCOUNTANT-only in owner UI/service.
+* DebtModule.open — DEBT_REPORT_VIEW, per its handoff.
+
+All factories use the existing production Service/DAO graph; no placeholders/fakes. Existing DashboardModule lifecycle,
+busy guards, session checks and Scene management remain in force. Home no longer says integrated modules are unavailable.
+
+## Approved compatibility fixtures
+
+Lead explicitly approved both test-only adaptations required by #25:
+
+1. MemoryBillingRepository.findChargesByApartment filters its invoice collection by apartment, sorts descending period,
+   and returns header snapshots. A new test verifies filtering/order/snapshot preservation without changing old assertions.
+2. NoticeServiceTest.Stub.getApartmentHistory does the same over its existing invoice map and retains scripted failures.
+
+No production contract/DAO/NoticeService was changed. The clean review branch deliberately omits @Override on these
+two incoming methods so the same fixtures compile both before and after #25. Signatures and behavior remain identical.
+
+## Full local integration regression
+
+JDK 17.0.17, Maven 3.9.9, Enforcer enabled. Every command completed BUILD SUCCESS, no skipped tests:
+
+| Profile | Tests | Failures | Errors | Skipped |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| normal | 699 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
+| javafx-smoke | 700 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
+| mysql-it | 832 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
+
+Commands used `-Dsurefire.useManifestOnlyJar=false`: default Windows manifest classpaths spanning V:/C: produced a
+Surefire fork error even after assertions ran. This runtime workaround changes neither tests, Enforcer nor pom.xml.
+Latest revision logs: original workspace `.tools/br02-revision-normal.log`, `br02-revision-javafx-smoke.log`,
+`br02-revision-mysql-it.log`. The final MySQL run was executed independently after an intermittent end-of-fork
+failure in the sequential-profile run; the independent run completed BUILD SUCCESS with all 832 tests.
+
+MySQL 8.4.0, isolated loopback port 33316, disposable `bluemoon_br02_test`, dedicated schema-scoped user and external
+ignored config. FK checks remained enabled. New fixtures guard `_test` before DDL, clean owned rows child-first,
+and only remove billing/payment tables absent on entry. Other suites passed in the full run.
+
+Verified real UI/MySQL:
+
+* Household production composition: saved invoice exists, Cancel leaves area 80, OK changes area to 95.50, invoice
+  remains byte-for-model equal; history still shows original snapshot area/total/due date. ACCOUNTANT reads; RESIDENT denied.
+* An authenticated real ACCOUNTANT records 23,000 VND through ReceiptService/ReceiptDAO against the fixture invoice.
+  Household Detail displays DONG_THIEU (Đóng thiếu), paid 23,000 and owing 100,000; snapshot total/area/people/due date stay unchanged.
+* BlueMoonApplication.start with real AuthService/AccountDAO and a disposable BCrypt account: Login → Dashboard →
+  Fee Rate/Billing/Notice/Payment/Debt → Home → Logout. Same Scene retained; session cleared.
+* Role menus/direct denial, duplicate opens, busy guards, disposal, DB-unavailable behavior covered by production-navigation
+  tests; existing AppShellTest/LoginUiTest cover maximize/restore and window-close handling.
+
+This is automated JavaFX/MySQL navigation coverage, not a manual business E2E claim for generating a period then
+recording a payment/exporting notices through every screen. New BR-02 UI tests use an issued invoice snapshot fixture;
+owner BillingMySqlIT separately verifies real generation and BR-02 lookup. Manual QA should still execute the full flow.
+
+## QA / merge order
+
+1. Review the clean composition/fixture PR on its own recorded regression. PO may merge it before #25; it intentionally
+   remains compatible with both versions and prevents #25 breaking Billing/Notice test compilation.
+2. PO merges approved #25. Create a clean BR-02 feature branch from updated main and transfer only the Household
+   UI/navigation/composition delta from the local integration, preserving Search and all five module registrations.
+   Re-run normal/smoke/full MySQL; do not push any composite dependency history as a PR.
+3. ADMIN: Household Detail → verify newest-first snapshot history → edit area → Cancel → verify unchanged → OK → verify
+   current area changes while old invoice totals/area remain unchanged. ACCOUNTANT can view; RESIDENT cannot access.
+4. Maximize/restore before switching modules; try navigation/logout while loading, writing and awaiting confirmation.
+   Stop only the disposable DB to verify sanitized errors/retry. Confirm old panels do not update after close/logout.
+5. ACCOUNTANT: preview/generate a test billing period, record partial/full payment, reload Debt, view/export Notice;
+   ADMIN may inspect payment but cannot record it. Test empty periods and repeated clicks.
+
+BR-02 acceptance: implemented and verified locally; **formal PR BLOCKED only by unmerged #25** at this snapshot.
+Composition: all five modules connected; clean PR verification tracked independently. No main merge performed by Dev-2.
